Wed Sep 16 18:56:00 UTC 2026 - koxt2 <koxt2@protonmail.com>

- Update to 0.6.0: Harden pkexec-helper and improve compatibility with Linux distros
  * Privileged ddrescue helper now derives ownership from `PKEXEC_UID`
  * Removed the Polkit `allow_gui` override
  * Hardened privileged operations against unsafe device paths and symbolic-link attacks
  * Added validation for device paths, output locations, ownership IDs, and temporary directories
  * Image and mapfile creation now uses private temporary directories and atomic moves

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Thu Sep 10 18:28:00 UTC 2026 - koxt2 <koxt2@protonmail.com>

- Update to 0.5.0-1: fix RPM lint errors
  * Removed setBadness('polkit-untracked-privilege', 0) from
    datarecovery-rpmlintrc
  * Added filter for hicolor-icon-theme
  * Removed Group: from spec file

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Tue Apr 28 21:21:00 UTC 2026 - koxt2 <koxt2@protonmail.com>

- Update to release 0.5.0
  * Progress bar updates while recovering data and organising files
  * New `utils.py` module with shared `format_bytes` and
    `format_size` functions
  * Disk space check now also runs when recovering from an image
    file (previously only ran for physical devices)
  * Logs are now always generated and saved to destination (no
    longer optional)
  * photorec progress can be displayed
  * Application no longer re-initialises when brought back to the
    foreground (subsequent activations now just re-present the
    existing window)
  * `MountedPartitionChecker` no longer takes an unused
    `device_dropdown` parameter
  * `PartitionRow.type` property renamed to `part_type` to avoid
    shadowing the Python built-in
  * Duplicate `/d` flag in PhotoRec command that would confuse file
    output location

-------------------------------------------------------------------
